  <string name="help_title">Help</string>
  <string name="help_adding_title">Adding an item</string>
  <string name="help_adding_text">Tap + on the main screen and enter the name and the expiry date: either the date from the package, or the production date and the shelf life. If the package shows only the month and year, the last day of that month is used.</string>
  <string name="help_opening_title">Shelf life after opening</string>
  <string name="help_opening_text">Many items keep for less time once opened. Tap “Open today” on the item card and the app recalculates the date: the opening date plus the shelf life after opening, but never later than the date on the package.\n\nThat is why the number of days left can drop after opening. If you marked it by mistake, tap “Undo opening”.</string>
  <string name="help_notifications_title">Notifications</string>
  <string name="help_notifications_text">Every day at the time you choose, the app checks the dates and reminds you about items that are about to expire. How many days in advance to remind is set for each item, and the default is chosen in Settings. Tap a notification to open the item.\n\nIf the app has not been opened for two days or more, a “While you were away” message above the list shows the items that expired in that time. If notifications are turned off in the phone settings, the main screen shows a warning with a “Turn on” button.</string>
  <string name="help_subscriptions_title">Subscriptions</string>
  <string name="help_subscriptions_text">On the Subscriptions tab you can keep track of paid subscriptions: the price, the billing period and a reminder before each charge. The total per month is shown above the list, and the next charge date is updated automatically.\n\nTap a subscription to edit, cancel or delete it. A cancelled subscription is not counted in the total and sends no reminders, but it stays under “Cancelled” and can be resumed.</string>
  <string name="help_account_title">Account and sync</string>
  <string name="help_account_text">Without an account your data is stored only on this phone. Once you sign in, it is saved on the server and appears on your other devices with the same account.\n\nTo sign out, tap “Sign out” in the profile. If some changes have not reached the server yet, the app will warn you.</string>

