  <string name="help_family_title">Family</string>
  <string name="help_family_text">On the Home tab you can keep a shared list with your family. Create a group and send the invite code, it is valid for 24 hours. All members see the items in the shared list, and everyone gets expiry reminders.\n\nThe group owner can remove a member, and a member can leave on their own. Personal items are not affected.</string>

  <string name="help_list_title">List and search</string>
  <string name="help_list_text">On the Expiry tab items are grouped into “Expired”, “Soon” and “Later”. The colour on the right shows urgency: red means the item has expired or expires today or tomorrow, yellow means within a week, green means there is still time.\n\nTap a category above the list to show only that category. You can delete your own category with a long press, its items will stay without a category. The magnifier icon opens search by name, and the menu next to it lets you choose the sort order and show only opened or only sealed items. The selected category, order and filter are kept until the next launch.</string>
  <string name="help_deleting_title">Deleting an item</string>
  <string name="help_deleting_text">When an item is used up or thrown away, delete it: tap the bin icon on the item card or long-press the row in the list. If the item is deleted before it expires, the statistics count it as used in time, and if after, as thrown away.</string>
  <string name="help_profile_title">Profile and settings</string>
  <string name="help_profile_text">The profile opens from the circle in the top right corner. It shows how many items are tracked, expire this week and have already expired, and how many were used in time and thrown away this month.\n\nIn Settings you choose the time of daily notifications, the default reminder for new items and subscriptions, the theme and the app language.</string>
